domain StructuredSemanticAuthoringKernelDesignV1Review:
  description "Evidence-chain re-review of D11 design candidate revision two."
problem P1:
  |
    Determine whether revision two still contains a present contract contradiction,
    unsafe authority allocation, or unresolved incompatible design choice. Do not
    reject it merely because downstream implementation detail remains unfinished.
evidence E1:
  |
    Accepted character requirement v5 R10 defines the semantic-skeleton checkpoint
    after identity, core goals, essential abilities or limits, and key relationships
    exist and before dependent prose and behavior fan out.
evidence E2:
  |
    Revision two lines 297 through 307 define a skeleton phase spanning cluster one
    and only server-designated essential ability or limit and key-relationship slices
    from clusters two and three; remaining dependent work fans out only after passage.
evidence E3:
  |
    Revision two lines 394 through 405 restrict set_skeleton to a closed operation
    subset and target keys registered in skeletonRequiredClaimIds, with no other
    cluster-two or cluster-three claim exposed.
evidence E4:
  |
    Accepted character requirement v5 R7 prohibits model invention of stable IDs.
    Revision two removes set_portrait from the operation catalog and lines 413 through
    417 preserve server ownership and reject provider selection of portrait IDs.
evidence E5:
  |
    Immutable comparison against revision-one Seal 522378793fa4 shows content changes
    are confined to revision status, the skeleton correction, portrait correction and
    self-review explanation.
evidence E6:
  |
    Revision two lines 781 through 787 retains exact DTO elaboration, takeover detail,
    fifteen-case traceability and complete public Q&A projection as downstream
    obligations, and retains four owner policy decisions without claiming acceptance.
evidence E7:
  |
    Command-line audit of revision-two design reasoning reports zero fatal, error and
    warning findings. Git whitespace validation and Sealgraph repository integrity
    checks pass.
premise C1:
  |
    A present REVISE finding requires a material conflict with accepted semantics or
    authority, or an incompatible unresolved choice that prevents reliance now.
premise C2:
  |
    A retained downstream obligation is not waived, but incomplete elaboration at its
    later gate is not a present design defect.
premise U1:
  |
    Provider convergence, numerical fitness, public compatibility selection, Q&A
    restart selection and detector tuning remain unverified or owner-controlled; this
    review does not convert them into findings.
decision D1 based_on P1, E1, E2, E3, C1:
  |
    The semantic-skeleton correction satisfies the accepted checkpoint ordering while
    retaining focused context and avoiding complete early cluster expansion.
decision D2 based_on P1, E4, C1:
  |
    The portrait correction restores server authority over stable media identifiers
    and leaves no model-writable portrait operation.
decision D3 based_on P1, E5, E6, C1, C2, U1:
  |
    No additional present blocker is established. The four detail items remain later
    completion obligations and the four policy alternatives remain owner decisions.
decision D4 based_on P1, D1, D2, D3, E7:
  |
    Report PASS with no P0 through P3 findings and recommend owner ACCEPT for this exact
    design revision. Do not infer implementation, provider, cutover or deployment
    authority from review success.
